    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just \"difficult\"... it's final. i see people on the street and i know they know. they've all read the news. the version of me that mattered is dead. there's no \"rebuilding\" from this. how do you even start over when the person everyone respected doesn't exist anymore? it feels like there's just no path forward.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the external self you knew is gone, the focus needs to shift inward to find a different kind of foundation. While the past cannot be recovered, starting over doesn't mean erasing everything; it means choosing what you want the *next* self to be, even if it feels small right now. Even tiny, deliberate actions can create a new path forward, and seeking therapeutic support can help you navigate this profound redirection of self.",
      "source": "target",
